cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NCMemSim in research, cite the exact software version and this repository."
title: "NCMemSim: Nanocrystal Memory Simulation Platform"
type: software
version: 1.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: Apache-2.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23078330
    description: "Concept DOI representing all published versions"
authors:
  - family-names: Cojocaru
    given-names: Ovidiu
repository-code: "https://github.com/ocojocaru/NCMemSim"
abstract: >-
  A modular Python framework for simulation and design-technology
  co-optimization of Ge/GeSn nanocrystal non-volatile memories,
  including multi-floating-gate state dynamics, compact electrostatics,
  local fields, WKB tunnelling, charge redistribution, retention,
  optical and electro-optical programming, experimental-data handling,
  deterministic parameter fitting, uncertainty diagnostics, calibration
  qualification, deterministic design-space sweeps, Pareto and grid sensitivity
  analysis, bounded independent uncertainty propagation, explicit robust objectives,
  reproducible nominal and Robust DTCO reports, immutable scientific workflow
  evidence, fitted evaluator contexts, linked workflow exports, opt-in trap-assisted
  transport with image-force barrier corrections, mechanism-resolved diagnostics and reports,
  reproducible stochastic nanocrystal ensembles, population statistics, feasibility and failure
  accounting, variability-aware DTCO, ensemble Pareto analysis, and integrity-checked ensemble
  reports, explicit model/TAT-density variability, isolated model execution, source-linked
  population and Pareto analysis, strict MODEL report bundles, opt-in reference-anchored
  Si and Ge temperature properties, isolated thermal simulation contexts, thermal DTCO,
  source-linked thermal report bundles, explicit broadband and discrete spectral sources,
  ordered single-pass optical propagation, spectral pulse contexts and strict spectral
  report bundles, validation, and reproducibility tools.
keywords:
  - nanocrystal memory
  - non-volatile memory
  - GeSn
  - floating gate
  - tunnelling
  - retention
  - DTCO
